WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.626 --> 00:00:10.173
I frequently miss entire days

00:00:11.299 --> 00:00:14.761
caught in my brain’s spider webs

00:00:15.762 --> 00:00:17.597
but if I happen to 
look up in time

00:00:17.597 --> 00:00:20.725
to notice that the darkness

00:00:20.725 --> 00:00:23.937
still has a little daylight
left to swallow

00:00:24.896 --> 00:00:29.109
I will ivy up the fire escape to catch

00:00:29.109 --> 00:00:32.112
whatever embers of the day

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.949
are still slow dying behind New Jersey

00:00:36.866 --> 00:00:39.035
and last week through the fog

00:00:39.035 --> 00:00:41.079
of my loneliness I realized

00:00:41.079 --> 00:00:44.124
the living room was slippery pink

00:00:44.124 --> 00:00:45.834
which I knew meant

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:48.003
a light show must be on display

00:00:48.545 --> 00:00:51.548
so with a quickness I reserve
for emergencies

00:00:51.548 --> 00:00:54.676
I scampered to the roof and sure enough

00:00:54.718 --> 00:00:59.431
an explosion of upside-down clementine

00:00:59.431 --> 00:01:01.975
cotton candy cloud wisps

00:01:02.017 --> 00:01:05.186
was tie-dyeing the Hudson River neon

00:01:05.228 --> 00:01:08.523
and I swear I am not a lightweight

00:01:08.565 --> 00:01:11.610
but I was colordrunk immediately

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:14.821
dizzy with gasp and skyward-reaching

00:01:14.863 --> 00:01:16.948
hoping my fingers might find

00:01:16.948 --> 00:01:18.908
a bell I could ring

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:21.911
that would summon all of New York City

00:01:21.911 --> 00:01:26.333
to look up! and west!

00:01:26.791 --> 00:01:29.878
but there was no bell and no one to call

00:01:29.878 --> 00:01:32.213
just my own astonishment

00:01:32.213 --> 00:01:35.383
still willing to answer
after the first ring

00:01:35.383 --> 00:01:38.845
how predictable:
one good sunset

00:01:38.845 --> 00:01:40.847
and I release my nihilism

00:01:40.847 --> 00:01:43.933
like rose petals behind a bridal gown

00:01:43.933 --> 00:01:47.854
look I have married my cynicism

00:01:47.896 --> 00:01:50.231
and renewed my vows

00:01:50.231 --> 00:01:52.192
but it didn’t stop the streetlights

00:01:52.192 --> 00:01:56.488
from coming on at the exact moment
I passed beneath them

00:01:56.655 --> 00:01:59.407
when nobody else
was in the park to see it

00:01:59.741 --> 00:02:02.077
like the whole city was winking

00:02:02.118 --> 00:02:04.037
and yes I blushed

00:02:04.037 --> 00:02:07.916
the way I do whenever someone
beautiful flirts with me

00:02:08.792 --> 00:02:11.836
I haven’t stopped thinking about death

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:16.174
I am just wringing every last jaw-drop

00:02:16.216 --> 00:02:19.302
from the tissue between heartbreaks

00:02:19.344 --> 00:02:22.347
On a long run outside the city

00:02:22.347 --> 00:02:24.099
along a highway and

00:02:24.099 --> 00:02:25.850
miles from any shoreline

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:31.731
I found a starfish alone on the asphalt

00:02:31.773 --> 00:02:34.567
an unsolvable mystery

00:02:34.567 --> 00:02:37.362
with no witness to corroborate

00:02:37.362 --> 00:02:39.531
and there I was again

00:02:39.572 --> 00:02:42.283
wandering the streets of

00:02:42.283 --> 00:02:44.202
Bewilderville: Population 1

00:02:44.244 --> 00:02:47.038
what else could I possibly do

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:50.208
but swing wide the doors of my delight

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:54.671
to this patron saint of unbelonging

00:02:54.671 --> 00:03:00.969
fragile and whole and so far from home

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:07.016
if you too have been
the one nobody asked to dance

00:03:07.016 --> 00:03:10.228
I’ve got a starfish
I’d love to introduce you to

00:03:11.104 --> 00:03:12.897
and I don’t have any proof

00:03:12.939 --> 00:03:14.524
but one time the wind

00:03:14.524 --> 00:03:18.862
or my ancestors or unseasonal warmth

00:03:19.279 --> 00:03:21.406
carried three hawks

00:03:21.573 --> 00:03:23.575
to my kitchen windowsill

00:03:23.616 --> 00:03:26.119
to rattle my coffin to cocoon

00:03:26.119 --> 00:03:27.537
and two of them left

00:03:27.579 --> 00:03:29.914
but one of them stayed

00:03:29.914 --> 00:03:31.374
eyed me through the glass

00:03:31.374 --> 00:03:35.211
like a promise or a dare

00:03:35.336 --> 00:03:38.757
and so lately I am trying

00:03:38.757 --> 00:03:40.133
to pick up

00:03:40.425 --> 00:03:43.011
when the universe calls

00:03:44.429 --> 00:03:47.807
(Applause)

